module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.AffineComponents
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.GenericFibre.ModelOverField
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.LocallyPrincipalSupport

/-!
# The Noetherian case of Stacks 053R in algebraic form

The last paragraph of the proof of Stacks 053R reduces the general case to the Noetherian case by
descending the following affine situation to a finitely generated `ℤ`-algebra: `A ⊆ B` a finitely
generated extension of domains, `g ∈ B`, and `𝔭` a prime of `A`, subject to

1. `A ⊆ B` is a finitely generated extension of domains;
2. the image of `g` in `B ⊗_A K` is invertible, where `K` is the fraction field of `A`;
3. `dim (B ⊗_A K) = dim (B ⊗_A κ(𝔭))`;
4. the image of `g` in `B ⊗_A κ(𝔭)` is not a unit;
5. the image of `g` in `B ⊗_A κ(𝔭)` lies in no minimal prime of `B ⊗_A κ(𝔭)`.

This file proves that **(1)–(5) are contradictory as soon as `B` is Noetherian**, which is
exactly what the descent is for: it replaces `A ⊆ B` by a finitely generated `ℤ`-algebra
`A₀ ⊆ B₀`, for which `B₀` *is* Noetherian, while preserving (1)–(5).

The contradiction is assembled from two halves already in the library. The Noetherian case of
053R, proved for schemes in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.LocallyPrincipalSupport`, is run at the morphism
`Spec B ⟶ Spec A` with the ideal sheaf cut out by `g`; conditions (2) and (3) supply its two
hypotheses through the affine fibre dictionary of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.AffineFibre`, and it concludes that the support of
`g` in the fibre over `𝔭` is a union of irreducible components of that fibre. Conditions (4) and
(5) say it is not, by
`PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_singleton_ne_sUnion_irreducibleComponents`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.isLocallyPrincipal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton`: the ideal sheaf cut out by a
  principal ideal of the global sections is locally principal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.coe_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_spec`: on `Spec B` its support is the
  zero locus of the generator.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isDominant_specMap_algebraMap`: `Spec B ⟶ Spec A` is dominant when
  `A → B` is injective.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing`:
  **the Noetherian case of Stacks 053R in algebraic form.** Under (1), (2) and the inequality
  half of (3), the support of `g` in `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B)` is the union of the irreducible
  components of that spectrum contained in it.
* `Stacks.Divisors.not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_isNoetherianRing`:
  **conditions (1)–(5) are contradictory when `B` is Noetherian.** This is the statement the
  descent to a finitely generated `ℤ`-algebra is designed to apply.
* `Stacks.Divisors.not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_finiteType_int`: the same with
  `B` Noetherian replaced by `A` of finite type over `ℤ`, which is the hypothesis the descent
  actually establishes.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_isUnit_and_le_and_not_isUnit`: non-vacuity — the
  hypotheses (1), (2) and (3) of the two theorems above are jointly satisfiable, by
  `A = B = ℚ[t]` with `g = t` and `𝔭 = (t)`, where (4) holds and (5) therefore must fail.

## What remains of the general case of Stacks 053R

One piece, not in this file.

* The passage from the scheme-level statement to the affine situation: reducing to `X`, `S`
  integral (053P, 01ON, 0356) and choosing simultaneous affine charts `U = Spec A ∋ s`,
  `V = Spec B ∋ x` with `f(V) ⊆ U` inside a principality chart of `I`.

The *descent* itself — given the situation (1)–(3) at `A ⊆ B`, producing a finitely generated
`ℤ`-subalgebra `A₀ ⊆ A` and the `A₀`-subalgebra `B₀ ⊆ B` generated by a chosen set of generators
for which (1)–(3) still hold, and transporting the conclusion back — is
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.AffineGeneralCase`, which therefore removes
`[IsNoetherianRing B]` from the statements below. Its ingredients are in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.FinitePresentation.FiniteTypeDescent`:
`MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq` chooses `A₀` and
`MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv` identifies the two fibres.

## Implementation notes

`ringKrullDim` appears in the hypotheses rather than `dim`, and (3) is weakened to the inequality
`dim (κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B) ≤ dim (K ⊗[A] B)`, which is all the scheme-level theorem uses and all the
descent has to preserve.

`g : B` is transported to a global section of `Spec B` by `(Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv`; the
resulting ideal sheaf is `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {·})`, whose support is
identified with `PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g}` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.coe_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_spec`.

Condition (2) and condition (4) are the same assertion at the two primes `⊥` and `𝔭`, namely
`PrimeSpectrum.not_isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_iff`; the emptiness of the generic fibre of the closed
subscheme, which is the scheme-level hypothesis, is condition (2) read through that equivalence
and `AlgebraicGeometry.genericPoint_eq_bot_of_affine`.

The algebra structure of `κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B` over `B` is `Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra`, enabled
here by `attribute [local instance]`; enable it the same way to use these statements.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053R)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-- The ideal sheaf cut out by a principal ideal of the global sections is locally principal: on
every affine open the ideal is generated by the restriction of the generator. -/
public theorem isLocallyPrincipal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton {X : Scheme.{u}} (g : Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    IsLocallyPrincipal (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {g})) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨U, hxU⟩ := exists_affineOpens_mem x
  refine ⟨U, hxU, ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  exact ⟨_, rfl⟩

end Stacks.Divisors

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- On `Spec B`, the support of the ideal sheaf cut out by the principal ideal generated by
`g : B` is the zero locus of `g`. -/
public theorem coe_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_spec (B : Type u) [CommRing B] (g : B) :
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.span {(Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv g})).support :
      Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of B))) = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_ofIdealTop, Scheme.zeroLocus_span,
    ← Set.image_singleton (f := (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv),
    Spec_zeroLocus_eq_zeroLocus]

/-- `Spec B ⟶ Spec A` is dominant when `A → B` is injective: the closure of the range of the
contraction map is the zero locus of the kernel, which is everything. -/
public theorem isDominant_specMap_algebraMap (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B] :
    IsDominant (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) := by
  rw [isDominant_iff]
  change DenseRange (PrimeSpectrum.comap (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)).hom)
  rw [DenseRange, dense_iff_closure_eq, PrimeSpectrum.closure_range_comap]
  simp only [CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
  rw [(RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mp (FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective A B)]
  exact PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_bot

/-- For the identity algebra structure the fibre ring is the residue field itself, so every fibre
of `Spec A ⟶ Spec A` has Krull dimension `0`. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_fiber_self (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : Ideal A) [p.IsPrime] :
    ringKrullDim (p.Fiber A) = 0 :=
  (ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.rid A A p.ResidueField).toRingEquiv).trans
    (ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_field _)

end AlgebraicGeometry

section Fibre

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B]
  [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B]

/-- **Stacks 053R, the Noetherian case, in the algebraic form the reduction to it consumes.** Let
`A ⊆ B` be a finitely generated extension of domains, let `g ∈ B`, and let `𝔭` be a prime of
`A`. Assume `B` is Noetherian, that the image of `g` in `K ⊗[A] B` is a unit, where `K` is the
fraction field of `A` (condition (2) of the source), and that the fibre over `𝔭` has dimension at
most that of the generic fibre (the inequality half of condition (3)). Then the support of `g` in
`Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B)` is the union of the irreducible components of that spectrum contained in
it.

This is the scheme-theoretic Noetherian case
`Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents` run at `Spec B ⟶ Spec A`, read
through the affine fibre dictionary. -/
public theorem zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing
    [IsNoetherianRing B] (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (h2 : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h3 : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B)) :
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g} :
        Set (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B))) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B)) |
        Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B)) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g}} := by
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) :=
    locallyOfFiniteType_specMap_algebraMap A B
  have : IsDominant (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) :=
    isDominant_specMap_algebraMap A B
  have hdomA : IsDomain (CommRingCat.of A) := ‹IsDomain A›
  set I : (Spec (CommRingCat.of B)).IdealSheafData :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.span {(Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv g}) with hIdef
  have hI : IsLocallyPrincipal I := isLocallyPrincipal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton _
  have hsupp : (I.support : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of B))) = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} :=
    coe_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_spec B g
  -- Condition (2) says no prime of `B` containing `g` contracts to the generic point of `Spec A`.
  have hgen : ∀ y ∈ (I.support : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of B))),
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) y ≠
        genericPoint (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) := by
    intro y hy hcon
    refine (PrimeSpectrum.not_isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_iff A B ⊥ g).mpr ⟨y, ?_, ?_⟩ h2
    · exact hcon.trans (genericPoint_eq_bot_of_affine (CommRingCat.of A))
    · exact (PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus _ _).mp (hsupp ▸ hy) (Set.mem_singleton _)
  have hgeneric : IsEmpty ((I.subschemeι ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber
        (genericPoint (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))) :=
    (I.isEmpty_fiber_comp_iff (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) _).mpr hgen
  -- Condition (3) is the dimension inequality through the dictionary.
  have hdim : topologicalKrullDim
        ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ≤
      topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber
        (genericPoint (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))) :=
    (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_specMap_eq A B p).trans_le
      (h3.trans (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_specMap_genericPoint_eq A B).ge)
  have hres := fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) I hI hgeneric p hdim
  exact (fiberSpecHomeo A B p).eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_image
    (fiberSpecHomeo_image_preimage_zeroLocus A B p g)
    ((congrArg ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹' ·) hsupp) ▸ hres)

/-- **Conditions (1)–(5) of the last paragraph of the proof of Stacks 053R are contradictory as
soon as `B` is Noetherian.** This is the statement the descent to a finitely generated
`ℤ`-algebra is designed to apply: it replaces `A ⊆ B` by `A₀ ⊆ B₀` with `B₀` of finite type over
`ℤ`, hence Noetherian, while preserving (1)–(5). -/
public theorem not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_isNoetherianRing
    [IsNoetherianRing B] (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (h2 : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h3 : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B))
    (h4 : ¬ IsUnit (algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h5 : ∀ Q ∈ minimalPrimes (p.asIdeal.Fiber B),
      algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g ∉ Q) : False :=
  PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_singleton_ne_sUnion_irreducibleComponents _ h4 h5
    (zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing g p h2 h3)

/-- **Why the descent to a finitely generated `ℤ`-algebra solves the problem.** Conditions
(1)–(5) of the last paragraph of the proof of Stacks 053R are contradictory as soon as `A` is of
finite type over `ℤ`: then `A` is Noetherian by the Hilbert basis theorem and `B`, of finite type
over `A`, is Noetherian too, so
`Stacks.Divisors.not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_isNoetherianRing` applies.

This is the exact shape the descent produces — `A₀` a finitely generated `ℤ`-subalgebra of `A`
and `B₀` the `A₀`-subalgebra of `B` generated by the chosen generators — so with this in hand the
residue of the general case of Stacks 053R is the descent itself: producing `A₀` for which
(1)–(5) still hold. -/
public theorem not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_finiteType_int
    [Algebra.FiniteType ℤ A] (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (h2 : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h3 : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B))
    (h4 : ¬ IsUnit (algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h5 : ∀ Q ∈ minimalPrimes (p.asIdeal.Fiber B),
      algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g ∉ Q) : False :=
  have : IsNoetherianRing A := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing ℤ A
  have : IsNoetherianRing B := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing A B
  not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_isNoetherianRing g p h2 h3 h4 h5

/-- **Non-vacuity.** Conditions (1), (2), (3) and (4) are jointly satisfiable, so
`Stacks.Divisors.not_isUnit_and_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes_of_isNoetherianRing` is not derived
from an empty hypothesis set: what it refutes is the conjunction of those four with (5).

The witness is `A = B = ℚ[t]` with the identity algebra structure, `g = t` and `𝔭 = (t)`. It is a
finitely generated extension of domains with `B` Noetherian, so (1) holds; `t` is invertible in
`K ⊗[A] A = K`, the fraction field, since `t ≠ 0`, so (2) holds; both fibre rings are residue
fields of `ℚ[t]`, of Krull dimension `0`, so (3) holds; and `t` lies in the prime `(t)` of the
fibre over `(t)`, so it is not a unit there and (4) holds. (5) must therefore fail, and it does:
`t` maps to `0` in the residue field at `(t)`, and `0` lies in every minimal prime. -/
public theorem exists_isUnit_and_le_and_not_isUnit :
    ∃ (p : PrimeSpectrum (Polynomial ℚ)) (g : Polynomial ℚ),
      IsUnit (algebraMap (Polynomial ℚ)
          ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum (Polynomial ℚ)).asIdeal.Fiber (Polynomial ℚ)) g) ∧
        ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber (Polynomial ℚ)) ≤
          ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum (Polynomial ℚ)).asIdeal.Fiber (Polynomial ℚ)) ∧
        ¬ IsUnit (algebraMap (Polynomial ℚ) (p.asIdeal.Fiber (Polynomial ℚ)) g) := by
  have hprime : (Ideal.span {Polynomial.X} : Ideal (Polynomial ℚ)).IsPrime :=
    (Ideal.span_singleton_prime Polynomial.X_ne_zero).mpr Polynomial.prime_X
  refine ⟨⟨Ideal.span {Polynomial.X}, hprime⟩, Polynomial.X, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← not_not (a := IsUnit _), PrimeSpectrum.not_isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_iff]
    rintro ⟨𝔮, h𝔮, hg⟩
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_self, PrimeSpectrum.comap_id] at h𝔮
    have h𝔮' : 𝔮 = (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum (Polynomial ℚ)) := h𝔮
    rw [h𝔮', PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal_bot] at hg
    exact Polynomial.X_ne_zero (Ideal.mem_bot.mp hg)
  · rw [AlgebraicGeometry.ringKrullDim_fiber_self, AlgebraicGeometry.ringKrullDim_fiber_self]
  · rw [PrimeSpectrum.not_isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_iff]
    refine ⟨⟨Ideal.span {Polynomial.X}, hprime⟩, ?_, Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_singleton _)⟩
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_self, PrimeSpectrum.comap_id]

end Stacks.Divisors

end Fibre

end
